//@version=5

// @description This library is a collec tion of assistence tools saving me the need to copy same code again and again in my various indicators and strategies.
library("LIB_TradeAssist")

// @function Calculate the slop magnetude betwen current price and an older price. Since the change is usually minimal, we multiply it by def value of 3000 to make it usable.You can optionally pass other multiply factor
// @param #1: val_now     - the most updated value
// @param #2: val_older   - older value to be compared against latest
// @param #3: mult_factor - Multiply factor to make very small numbers as  0.0034 usable. By default it use multiply factor of 3000. However you can assign any other value whenever required
// @returns : Slop angle magnetude
export Slop_Magnitude(float val_now, float val_older, float mult_factor = 3000) =>
	// Find Slop dir by calc arc-tangent betwen last two readings which gives the angle /_ in radian. To get angle in degree
	// we need to multiply by 180/Pi. Since the angle change is very very very small, we will multiply by ANGLE_X_FACT, easing user
	// dead zone confifuration (yellow). Dead zone is whenever change in angle is to small to report up or down (green/red) 
	math.atan(val_now - val_older) * mult_factor / math.pi


// @function - calculate moving average using one of the above - S MA, EMA, WMA, ALMA, RMA, VWMA, 
// @param #1: - Moving average type string: "SMA", "EMA", "WMA", "ALMA", "RMA", "VWMA"  
// @param #2: - price
// @param #3: - moving average length
// @returns : - Moving average value
export moving_avg(simple string ma_type, simple float price, simple int length) =>
    if ma_type == "SMA"
        ta.sma(price, length)
    else if ma_type == "EMA"
        ta.ema(price, length)
    else if ma_type == "WMA"
        ta.wma(price, length)
    else if ma_type == "ALMA"
        ta.alma(price, length, 0.85, 6)
    else if ma_type == "RMA"
        ta.rma(price, length)
    else if ma_type == "VWMA"
        ta.vwma(price, length)  //vwma is as if we wrote: sma(source * volume, length) / sma(volume, length).
    else
        na

